    {
      "id": "mZGcvC0JGTpcCdvBwWAxC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -756.6353632801124,
      "y": 1567.8640530459472,
      "width": 935,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#e9ecef",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 899226671,
      "version": 1200,
      "versionNonce": 1444719716,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790794584515,
      "created": 1790589539728,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Reads all the args ignoring the loader + flags unless found a sequence before a flag.\nthen some how it will combine all those numbers into one single array of integers.\n\nexample of behavior: \n- read args\n- ignore loader\n- ignore flags (if found)\n- joins all the strings in one single string using space as a separator\n- the splitting them into mini strings\n- iterates `atoi` function on them\n- vola... you have an array of integers.\n\nit might not be the best extracting behavior, discuss more later. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Reads all the args ignoring the loader + flags unless found a sequence before a flag.\nthen some how it will combine all those numbers into one single array of integers.\n\nexample of behavior: \n- read args\n- ignore loader\n- ignore flags (if found)\n- joins all the strings in one single string using space as a separator\n- the splitting them into mini strings\n- iterates `atoi` function on them\n- vola... you have an array of integers.\n\nit might not be the best extracting behavior, discuss more later. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
